=== TESTED SURFACE ===
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/entities?n=
               element kinds: entity
               EntityModel carries revealed_chapter directly.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/graph?n=
               element kinds: graph_node, graph_edge, graph_node_property
               Cytoscape elements; node.properties is a bare key->value dict with no reveal stamp on the wire, so it is resolved back to node_properties rows read-only.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/entity/{id}?n=
               element kinds: detail_entity, detail_edge, detail_property
               Requested for EVERY node id of the work at every chapter, so a not-yet-revealed id must 404 rather than serve; a 200 on an unrevealed id is itself a violation.
  [TESTED    ] GET /works/{slug}/arcs?n=
               element kinds: arc_name
               Arcs carry no revealed_chapter. Their fence rule (F6) is name redaction: an arc with start_chapter > n must send name=null. That rule is what is checked.
  [not tested] GET /works/{slug}/search?n=&q=
               element kinds: -
               NOT TESTED: the vector store directory (.chroma) does not exist in this checkout, so there is no index to query and the route cannot be exercised without first building one. Its fence key is chunk chapter_ordinal <= n.
  [not tested] GET /works/{slug}/status?n/a
               element kinds: -
